---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---
<section id="how-it-works" class="section container" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
  <div class="section-split">
    <SectionHeading index="03" label="The architecture" title="Local authority. Remote inference." id="architecture-title" />
    <p class="section-aside">Two clear responsibilities, connected through an authenticated worker endpoint.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="architecture">
    <div class="architecture-flow">
      <div class="architecture-node">
        <p class="node-label"><Icon name="monitor" /> ON YOUR PC</p>
        <h3>FreeCompute CLI + Core</h3>
        <p class="node-subtitle">Your workspace. Your authority.</p>
        <ul><li>File reads and approved edits</li><li>Approved commands and tests</li><li>Permissions, sessions and undo</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="architecture-link" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Authenticated connection</span>
        <div class="flow-out"><span>Model input</span><Icon name="arrow" /></div>
        <div class="flow-back"><Icon name="arrow" /><span>Text + tool proposals</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="architecture-node">
        <p class="node-label"><Icon name="server" /> ON YOUR WORKER</p>
        <h3>Model + GPU</h3>
        <p class="node-subtitle">llama.cpp + authenticated supervisor</p>
        <ul><li>Receives inference messages</li><li>Runs the configured model</li><li>Returns text and proposed tool calls</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>The worker proposes tool calls. The local Core validates and executes them, with approval for changes and commands. Use HTTPS or a secure private transport for the connection.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="architecture-footnote"><span class="mono">THE BOUNDARY</span> The worker processes model input. It does not operate your local terminal or access your project directly.</p>
</section>
